DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     llcc lists the files in each named _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y, or in the cur-
     rent directory if none is named.  Unless one of -bb, -cc, -dd,
     -ff, -mm, or -pp restricts the listing to one type, all six
     types are listed, each under its own heading (``Direc-
     tories'', ``Files'', ``Character special files'', ``Block
     special files'', ``Pipes'', ``Multiplexed files''), sorted
     by name and packed into columns that fit the terminal width.
     When more than one _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y is given, each is preceded by
     its own name.

     -11   List one file name per line instead of packing them
          into columns.

     -aa   Include .  and ..  in the listing.

     -bb   List block-special files only.

     -cc   List character-special files only.

     -dd   List directories only.

     -ff   List regular files only.

     -mm   List multiplexed (multiplexor) files only.  This option
          is accepted by the program but is not mentioned in its
          built-in usage message or in the Options table above.

     -pp   List pipe files only.

